---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Josh Turknett | Brains, Banjos, & Beyond" currentPage="home">

  <!-- Hero: Full viewport with background image -->
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-bg">
      <img src="/images/josh-performing2.png" alt="" data-parallax="0.3" class="hero-img-home" />
    </div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1 class="hero-title">The power of every brain is far greater than you realize.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Neurologist. Researcher. Author. Musician.</p>
      <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSepeh4_qQ-c7JIREBXz2arKyCH9RwFM0-7z7bNjH5roZF3WXQ/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta">Inquire about speaking</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core idea section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <p class="statement statement--center">
          Most of us underestimate what we're capable of—and what others are capable of—because we've been taught the wrong things about how learning works.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Institute for Performance Neurology -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="text-align: center;">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>The Institute for Performance Neurology</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width: 720px; margin: 1.5rem auto 2rem;">
          I founded the Institute for Performance Neurology to build a new field—the science of how people build, deploy, and sustain capability across a lifetime. It's where the research, the programs, and the framework behind all of this work live.
        </p>
        <a href="https://performanceneurology.institute" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta">Visit the Institute</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Speaking preview with split layout -->
  <section class="section section--gray">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split-image fade-in">
          <img src="/images/concert-vertical.jpg" alt="Josh Turknett performing live" style="object-fit: cover; object-position: center 25%; transform: scale(1.8); transform-origin: center 30%;" />
        </div>
        <div class="split-content fade-in fade-in-delay-1">
          <h2>Speaking</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            I talk to organizations about human capability—what actually limits it, what expands it, and why most of us have been getting the answer wrong.
          </p>
          <p>
            The talk weaves together science and live musical performance—ideas and artistry in conversation. The music isn't separate from the message. It's the message made audible.
          </p>
          <a href="/speaking" class="cta cta--outline">Learn more</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Books section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="fade-in" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Books</h2>
      <div class="books-grid">
        <div class="book-card fade-in fade-in-delay-1">
          <div class="book-cover">
            <img src="/images/book-anyone-can-play-music.jpg" alt="Anyone Can Play Music book cover" />
          </div>
          <h3>Anyone Can Play Music</h3>
          <p>Musical ability is a skill, not a gift. The brain mechanisms that support it remain available across the lifespan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="book-card fade-in fade-in-delay-2">
          <div class="book-cover">
            <img src="/images/book-genius-impostor.jpg" alt="The Genius and the Impostor book cover" />
          </div>
          <p class="book-meta">Available now</p>
          <h3>The Genius and the Impostor</h3>
          <p><em>The Neuroscience of Unlocking Human Potential</em></p>
          <p>Intelligence, like musical skill, is constructed through learning. It's not a fixed quantity you're born with.</p>
          <a href="https://geniusandimpostor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta cta--outline" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Get the book</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem;" class="fade-in">
        <a href="/books" class="cta cta--outline">All books</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Full-bleed image break -->
  <section class="image-section image-section--overlay">
    <img src="/images/concert-playing.jpg" alt="" data-parallax="0.2" />
    <div class="image-section-content">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="statement" style="color: white;">
          Music is my laboratory. It's where the theory meets practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Music preview -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split split--reverse">
        <div class="split-content fade-in">
          <h2>Music</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Everything I say about learning and the brain gets tested here—in performance, in teaching, in helping adults learn things they'd given up on.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Brainjo method applies what we know about neuroplasticity to adult music learning. Thousands of people worldwide have used it to discover they were wrong about what they could learn.
          </p>
          <a href="/music" class="cta cta--outline">Explore music</a>
        </div>
        <div class="split-image fade-in fade-in-delay-1">
          <img src="/images/josh-portrait.jpg" alt="Josh Turknett with banjos" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing statement -->
  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container" style="text-align: center;">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <p class="statement statement--center" style="color: white; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          When you understand how learning actually works, what you're capable of changes. I've seen it happen thousands of times.
        </p>
        <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSepeh4_qQ-c7JIREBXz2arKyCH9RwFM0-7z7bNjH5roZF3WXQ/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta">Inquire about speaking</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
